.TH CEXTRACT 1 "2024-01-15" "ctools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cextract \- extract concepts from sessions into files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cextract
.RB [ \-f
.IR format ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR strategy ]
.RB [ \-F
.IR filter ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I source
.RI [ destination ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cextract
(context copy) copies concepts between agent sessions and concept files.
Concepts are constraints, goals, preferences, observations, and references
that can be extracted from agent sessions and stored as individual JSON files.
.PP
The @ prefix denotes a session reference (agent/session_id).
Plain paths are concept JSON files.
Directories (ending with /) contain one concept file per concept.
.PP
Concepts are lines in the format:
"Use the following <type>: <text>"
where type is constraint, goal, preference, observation, or reference.
.PP
When the output target is a directory, each concept is written as a separate
JSON file. This makes concepts independently manipulable: include or exclude
by adding/removing files, merge by copying between directories, modify by
editing the JSON, and share via git or any file transfer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format
.I format
Set output format: json, xml, or md.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-strategy
.I strategy.json
Use a custom chunking strategy for concept extraction.
A strategy defines the LLM host, model, API key, and extraction prompt.
Without this flag, cextract uses regex pattern matching on conversation messages.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-filter
.I filter.json
Select which extracted concepts are kept. The file can be a built-in
filter (type/substring match), a JSON-RPC filter, or a decision-model
filter that scores each concept with a local Ollama model.
On any error a filter passes the concept through.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I sources
One or more sources:
.RS
.TP
.BI @ agent / session_id
Agent session to extract concepts from.
.TP
.I concept.json
JSON file containing concepts to inject.
.TP
.I concepts/
Directory of concept JSON files to inject.
.RE
.TP
.I destinations
One or more destinations:
.RS
.TP
.BI @ agent / session_id
Agent session to inject concepts into.
.TP
.I concept.json
JSON file to write extracted concepts to.
.TP
.I concepts/
Directory to write one concept file per concept.
.RE
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Dump to stdout
Extract concepts from a session and print to stdout as JSON (no destination):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cextract @opencode/ses_abc
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Extract to directory
Extract concepts from a session, one file per concept:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cextract @opencode/ses_abc concepts/
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Extract to file
Extract concepts from a session to a single JSON file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cextract @opencode/ses_abc concepts.json
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Inject
Inject concepts from files into a session:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cextract constraints.json @opencode/ses_abc
cextract concepts/ @opencode/ses_abc
cextract a.json b.json @opencode/ses_abc
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Session-to-session
Copy concepts from one session to another:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cextract @opencode/ses_abc @claude/ses_xyz
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Custom strategy
Use an LLM-based extraction strategy:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cextract --strategy my-strategy.json @opencode/ses_abc concepts/
.fi
.RE
.SH STRATEGIES
A strategy is a JSON file that defines how to extract concepts using an LLM:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "host": "http://localhost:11434",
  "model": "qwen2.5:3b",
  "api_key": null,
  "prompt": "Extract the key concepts from this conversation..."
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Different strategies can produce different concept chunkings.
Ontology is inherently contestable depending on framing, so strategies
allow users to define their own extraction approach.
.SH FILTERS
A filter selects which extracted concepts are kept.
The config file can be a built-in filter, a JSON-RPC filter, or a
decision-model filter.
.PP
Built-in (no server needed):
.PP
.RS
.nf
{ "types": ["constraint", "goal"], "exclude_types": ["reference"], "prompt": "ssl" }
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decision model: a small local classifier scores each concept and passes it
through only when confident. The endpoint field selects how the model is
asked:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemone  (default)  Ollama's typed /v1/systemone endpoint. Sends the state
                      and typed questions; returns a calibrated probability
                      per option. No free text, nothing to parse. Requires a
                      server with the typed endpoint (e.g. Ollama 0.40.x). noul mode gates on threshold.
chat                    Any OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions server
                      (vLLM, older Ollama, any gateway). Renders the question
                      as a lettered decision task and parses the model's
                      letter. Works with models that follow instructions;
                      raise max_tokens for thinking models.
.fi
.RE
.PP
.nf
{ "type": "systemone", "model": "tev1", "endpoint": "systemone",
  "instructions": "Is this concept about cryptography, secrets, or security?",
  "threshold": 0.6 }

{ "type": "systemone", "host": "http://vllm:8000", "model": "an-instruct-model",
  "endpoint": "chat", "max_tokens": 2048, "api_key": "...",
  "instructions": "Is this concept about cryptography, secrets, or security?" }
.fi
.PP
A multi-way question routes concepts by category; the concept passes only
when the model's choice is in the allowed list (the letter maps to a criteria
key on the chat endpoint):
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "type": "systemone",
  "model": "nimble",
  "mode": "choice",
  "question_name": "category",
  "instructions": "Which category does this concept belong to?",
  "criteria": { "coding": "style rules", "security": "secrets, crypto" },
  "allowed": ["coding", "security"]
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extra fields: question_name (default relevant), max_tokens (chat, default
2048), api_key (chat, sent as a Bearer token when set), and timeout seconds
(default 30). A config with a model and no command is a decision-model filter
even without an explicit type. On any error a filter passes the concept
through.
.SH CONCEPT FORMAT
Concepts are JSON objects with these fields:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "type": "constraint",
  "description": "programming language",
  "short": "Use Python 3.11+",
  "medium": "Use Python 3.11 or later with type hints",
  "long": "Use Python 3.11 or later with full type hints..."
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The tool extracts concepts from messages matching the pattern:
"Use the following <type>: <text>"
.SH EXAMPLES
Dump concepts to stdout (for testing/inspection):
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract @opencode/ses_abc123
[
  {
    "type": "constraint",
    "description": "Use C17 standard",
    "short": "Use C17 standard for all code",
    ...
  }
]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract concepts to a directory (one file per concept):
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract @opencode/ses_abc123 concepts/
Extracted 5 concepts to concepts/ (5 files)
$ ls concepts/
constraint_0aa712d89fbb067a.json
preference_a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8.json
observation_x9y8z7w6v5u4t3s2.json
goal_m1n2o3p4q5r6s7t8u9.json
reference_v0w1x2y3z4a5b6c7d8.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract concepts to a single file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract @opencode/ses_abc123 concepts.json
Extracted 3 concepts to concepts.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inject concepts into a session:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract concepts/ @opencode/ses_abc123
Injected 5 concepts into opencode/ses_abc123
.fi
.RE
.PP
Copy concepts between sessions:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract @opencode/ses_abc123 @claude/ses_xyz789
Copied 5 concepts to claude/ses_xyz789
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a custom extraction strategy:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract --strategy my-strategy.json @opencode/ses_abc123 concepts/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Filter concepts with a local decision model (keeps only the concepts the
model scores as relevant at or above the threshold):
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ cextract --filter security.json @opencode/ses_abc123 concepts/
Extracted 2 concepts to concepts/ (2 files)
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db
OpenCode SQLite database (reads/writes system messages).
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl
Claude Code session files (reads/writes system messages).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unknown agent, session not found, or invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cdir (1),
.BR cgrep (1),
.BR cdu (1)
